<title>USA: Hancock revises stock buyback program.</title>
<headline>Hancock revises stock buyback program.</headline>
<dateline>GULFPORT, Miss. 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hancock Holding Co said Thursday it had revised its stock buyback program to limit the number of shares it can buy under the program.</p>
<p>The company said it will buy back only those shares necessary to meet the requirements of its various compensation and benefit plans and future acquisitions.</p>
<p>Terms of the original buyback program were not provided in the company's statement.</p>
<p>Hancock, through its banks, operates banking offices and automated teller machines.</p>
